    <item>
      <title>As an Ingress Controller with Tyk Operator</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/nightly/tyk-on-prem/kubernetes-ingress/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/nightly/tyk-on-prem/kubernetes-ingress/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Ingress is an API object that manages external access to the services in a cluster, typically HTTP (source &lt;a href=&#34;https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/services-networking/ingress/&#34; class=&#34;external-links&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34; &gt;kubernetes.io - ingress&lt;/a&gt;).&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;Tyk Operator&lt;/strong&gt; offers an &lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/docs/nightly/product-stack/tyk-operator/tyk-ingress-controller/&#34;&gt;Ingress Controller&lt;/a&gt;, which dynamically manages Tyk ApiDefinition resources as per the ingress spec.&#xA;This way your &lt;strong&gt;Tyk Gateway&lt;/strong&gt; is configured as a drop-in replacement for a standard Kubernetes Ingress.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tyk Operator&lt;/strong&gt; is also the preferred way to use Tyk for users who follow GitOps standards. It enables Tyk to be used for managing API Definitions, security policies and other Tyk features.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
